  "obligation": "Execute array.fill/copy in the single VM, with packed normalization, graph-aware source covariance, overlap semantics and complete pre-write traps.",
  "representation": "One original graph-owned array field/storage projection serves length, fill and copy. Storage subtype is shared by lowering and live cross-owner checks. Fill normalizes once through existing storage semantics. Both ranges are checked through the shared range owner before mutation. Self-copy uses in-place overlap semantics; distinct owners copy directly without a temporary vector or collector re-entry. Two opcodes reuse the existing register-pair operand/root representation. Format64 admits the appended vocabulary without changing packed widths. No cell, side map, executor or duplicate conformance unit.",
  "scope": "230 matching affected pinned files, 30 focused directives and19 Node observations. Focused scope includes packed truncation, both overlap directions, immutable sources, empty boundary slices, unsigned bounds/null traps without partial writes, subtype reference copies, copied payload survival after source release and50000 allocations, and imported mutations/copies across shifted original graphs. Copy pinned cases remain masked by unported segment-backed constructors; no complete copy suite claim. No full Test262 or full Wasm suite, expectations/skips/inventory changes.",
